> ACTION - Till - Write a PDF page manipulation library GSoC project
>   - scope may be simply investigation and design spec
>
> I'm pretty sure Google only wants projects that do produce code.

I cannot find it now but I remember reading that they explicitly exclude
documentation work.

Daniel

PS: To add to what Till said, in general google tries to allocate one
student for every six applications. Each organisation is guaranteed 2
students, more are allocated if you get more applications. In our case the
LF clearly gets more than 2 students (actually 12) so we must have got ~60+
applications(or google thought it was important to prioritise LF work).
Essentially open printing is being subsidised by the other, more sexy,
linux foundation workgroups...

